              "text": "こうかいする (kōkai suru) is Sino-Japanese (kango) kōkai with the native verb suru, \"to do\": two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are kō, \"later\" (Middle Chinese huwX) and kai, \"regret\" (xwojH) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
